<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Where do you set the Master Value?</div></blockquote>To change master output power. Go to a channel that is set to master, then change the output.<br><blockquote class="uncited"><div>I want the value to be 5 watts all the time since I am not in a metro area by default I will need the full 5 watts to hit the repeaters.</div></blockquote>Then you don't need to do anything with the master. just set the power output of the channels to 5 watts.<br><blockquote class="uncited"><div>in the cps I changed a second value to 2/2/5 and it defaulted to 2 watts. </div></blockquote>That is correct, your radio output maximum is 5 watts, so the first number is your output.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5068">KA1CM</a> — Thu May 15, 2025 8:33 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
