<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Where do you set the Master Value?<br><br>I want the value to be 5 watts all the time since I am not in a metro area by default I will need the full 5 watts to hit the repeaters.<br><br>In the cps channel configuration I set one channel to Master and it used the value of 1 watt, in the cps I changed a second value to 2/2/5 and it defaulted to 2 watts.  I am lazy and guess I would like the channel set to 5 watts( since most of the time that is required) and lower it when the instances.<br><br>I am very new to DMR and codeplug programming, but the only time I can see using anything under 5 watts is 250mw to access the hot spot. So i would really like to have the 5watts programmed in the radio when I change that channel, instead of using the radio and going into the radio channel confige to change it temporarily.</div></blockquote>The power settings in the CPS is used for all three radio types with max 5W, 10W and 40W.<br><br>So for your 5W radio you should use this setting to get 5W on a channel by default (overriding master power)<br><div class="inline-attachment"><dl class="file"><dt class="attach-image"><img src="http://localhost/opengd77/download/file.php?id=2978&amp;sid=b9071b536aa83adf8f8d1214d7b81ce2" class="postimage" alt="Screenshot 2025-05-15 212723.jpg" onclick="viewableArea(this);" /></dt></dl></div><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Thu May 15, 2025 7:31 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
